# Publish the reviewed change

Part of the Workbench delivery workflow. Requires GitHub access (`gh` CLI or a connected GitHub MCP tool) — ask the user to set one up if neither is available.

1. Resolve the exact repository, task-owned branch, remote, PR and base. Read the repository PR guidance and template. Preserve unrelated edits and verify ownership before publication.
2. Freeze accepted requirements with `workbench.requirements_set`. Capture and record current content-bound verification and independent review with `workbench.evidence_capture` and `workbench.progress`. Stage only the selected task changes. Changed content, base or requirements require affected checks again.
3. Call `workbench.publication_prepare` with the current task revision, worker chat ID and exact authorized actions (`commit`, `push`, `pr`, or a narrower subset). Supply the selected staged paths, commit message and reviewed PR title/body. Follow [PR visual evidence](../../references/visual-evidence.md): include supported attachment paths/digests or verified asset URLs, plus relevant Storybook links. Report unsupported uploads before publication.
4. Call `workbench.publication_execute` once per authorized next step, using the latest task revision. The controller owns ordinary commits with hooks, ordinary pushes and draft-PR creation or managed body updates. It preserves existing readiness and human body text. Do not replace controller steps with manual commit, push or PR mutation commands.
5. If the attempt is running or uncertain, call `workbench.publication_reconcile` before any retry. It must confirm the exact result or prove a commit/push was unperformed. Preserve uncertain results, inspect the concrete blocker and obtain direct user review before closing the local attempt. A saved attempt grants no new authority.
6. Read back the confirmed head, base, PR readiness, final body, screenshot assets and Storybook links. Use `workbench.pr_refresh` to separate observed checks, required CI, human review and mergeability. Report local proof and pending or unavailable CI separately. Read [delivery evidence and recovery](../../references/delivery-recovery.md) for the complete tool contract.

Don't post review replies, notify anyone, change the PR base, merge, or deploy unless separately asked to. If you were only authorized to commit (not push), stop there.

**Next:** `workbench-greenlight <PR>` to handle CI results and review comments as they come in.

When publication is authorized, use Workbench publication prepare/execute/reconcile tools for the exact task. They require current content-bound verification and review. Never replace uncertain controller operations with manual commits, pushes or PR creation. If the tools are unavailable, preserve work and report the capability gap.
